CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*cscfg_mgr)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct cscfg_manager)...)
#490: FILE: drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-syscfg.c:154:
+	cscfg_mgr = kzalloc(sizeof(struct cscfg_manager), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

